##########################################################################
# AceCommander-ApplicationRelease - BuildMaster OtterScript Plan
#
# !! EDITING THIS FILE IS NOT ENOUGH - SYNC IT TO THE RAFT !!
#   BuildMaster executes the copy of this plan stored in its raft, NOT this
#   file. Committing a change here does nothing until you run:
#       Sync-BuildMasterPlans -Path <thisFile> -ApplicationName 'AceCommander-ReleaseBundle'
#   This plan is application-scoped to AceCommander-ReleaseBundle (Application_Id
#   1003) as raft item 3012; its pipeline is item 3013. An unscoped
#   Rafts_GetRaftItems query does NOT list them, which is how a 2026-09-04 audit
#   wrongly concluded the pipeline was empty.
#   The paired stage runner (Invoke-ApplicationReleaseStage.ps1) IS read from disk
#   at run time, so a commit that changes both leaves the raft passing the OLD
#   argument list to the NEW parameter block. When the missing argument is a
#   [Parameter(Mandatory)] one, PowerShell prompts a console that nobody can
#   answer and the stage HANGS FOREVER with no error - build stuck 'active', log
#   ending at "Executing pwsh...", near-zero CPU, and no
#   _generated/buildmaster/<BuildMasterBuildId>/ directory.
#   This cost a release cycle on 2026-08-03 in the PowerShellModule pipeline.
#   Root cause, triage checklist, and fail-fast guidance:
#       SolutionDocumentation/BuildMaster-Plan-Raft-Sync-Requirement.md
##########################################################################
# Commander-only thin adapter. Same Exec/>> literal shape as deployed CSharpPackage-5Stage.otter.
# No database apply, rebuilding above Experimental, service mutation, or distribution.
set $ReleaseBuildId = $BuildMasterId(build);
InedoCore::Exec
(
    FileName: pwsh,
    Arguments: >>-NonInteractive -File "$ApplicationReleaseRunner" -ContextPath "$ApplicationReleaseContext" -ExpectedContextSha256 "$ApplicationReleaseContextSha256" -Stage "$PipelineStageName" -BuildId "$ReleaseBuildId">>,
    WorkingDirectory: $ApplicationReleaseWorkingDirectory,
    SuccessExitCode: 0
);
